        <head>OCAL INTELLIGENCE.</head>
        <p>OCAL INTELLIGENCE.</p>
        <p>ThLiberal Federation Postponed. that"kNational Liberal Federation announce 1)4„e annual meeting, Which was to have, 7ld in Manchester on November 19th and 4 Postponed, Ur , Save the Fragments! tor gadeley, The Museum, Bold-street, begs berelees Of materials, which many people will .eft over from their sewing. The smal- ra'aLl,Pleces can be utilised, as quilts are being `e for distress in readiness for the winter. GYlnnastie Enthusiasts. 84,1: Whiter session at the Borough Gymna- The tV,4841 enthusiastically commenced last week. 41)0,11.1:1 attendance at the various classes was a figure which, it is expected, will nioased considerably during the following i 4410'1. awing to the war, the men's class s 'el. an usual. Liberal Bowlers. htthe",'e final of the President's main, played sure Liberal Club on Saturday, J. Stanley was eil stal in winning the premier prize, heat- The l'(*ney after a hard struggle in the final. toils well-known trundler, J. Graham, won the ,tlarpolat,icat competition. after defeating, j net,,l,4 'll the final. The prizes will be distri- - at a later date.</p>
