        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. EUROPEAN WAR. TOBACCO FUND FOR THE 2sn SOUTH LANCASHIRES (THE WARRINGTON LINE BATTALION) SERVING AT THE FRONT. At the request of several of my fellow towns- men I have pleasure in opening a fund for supplying the men of the 2nd South Lancashire Regiment serving at the Front with Pipes, Tobacco, and Cigarettes. The goods,will be shipped under the care of the War Office, free of all customs duty, and by the courtesy of the French and Belgian Govern- ments will be delivered free of all charges. It is proposed to despatch the first consign- ment on Monday, the sth of October, and sub- scriptions to the "Tobacco Fund" should be sent to the Borough Treasurer before that date. PETER PEACOCK, Mayor.</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. WAR REFUGEES. At the request of the Local Government Board, a War Refugees Committee has been appointed to make provision for the housing and maintenance of some of the Refugees from Belgium whose homes have been destroyed. The Committee have accepted the offer of Mr. Robert Pierpoint of the use of St. Austin's, Bold-street. Funds are urgently required, and I earnestly appeal for subscriptions. Gifts or Loans of Beds, Bed Linen, Furniture, Clothing, and offers of Food are solicited. Members of the Committee will be in attend- ance daily (Sunday and Saturday excepted), at St. Austin's, from 11 a.m. to 12.30 p.m., and from 3 to 4 p.m. Any lady or gentleman willing to accommo- date and maintain any of the Refugees in their own homes or elsewhere are invited to com- municate with the Town Clerk. Subscriptions to the "War Refugees Fund" should be sent to the Borough Treasurer, at Bank House. PETER PEACOCK, Mayor.</p>
