        <p>LANCASHIRE MICHAELMAS QUARTER SESSIONS. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the GENERAL QUARTER SESSIONS OF THE PEACE for the County of Lancaster will be holden at the Castle of Lancaster on Monday, the 19th October, 1914, at Eleven o'clock in the forenoon; and by adjournment at the following places and times, viz. At the Court House, in Preston, on Wednes- day, the 21st October, 1914, at Ten o'clock in the forenoon. • At the Assize Courts, in Manchester, on Monday, the 26th October, 1914, at half-past Ten o'clock in the forenoon. At the County Sessions House, in Liverpool, on Tuesday, the 3rd November, 1914, at half-past Ten o'clock in the forenoon. The Solicitors engaged in Prosecutions at the said Sessions are requested to take notice that all Depositions and Instructions for indictments are required to be sent to the Clerk of the Peace's Office seven days at least before the said sessions respectively. HARCOURT E. CLARE, Clerk of the Peace. Clerk of the Peace's Office, Preston. September, 1914.</p>
